models=[('Number station','Mr Aliyu puts 4 counters down. He touches each once: 1, 2, 3, 4. Then he adds 2: 5, 6. So 4 + 2 = 6. Grace checks by moving each counter once.', 'Put 3 counters down. Add 2. Count them together. Explain how you avoid counting one twice.','5 counters; touch or move each once.',[3,2,5]),('Part station','Mr Aliyu puts 7 counters down. He moves 3 away. 4 remain: 7 - 3 = 4. He checks 3 + 4 = 7. Adamu makes sure each friend can see.','Put 8 counters down. Move 2 away. Say the remaining number. Check by putting the parts together.','6 remain; 2 + 6 = 8.',[8,-2,6]),('Compare and shape station','Mr Aliyu aligns the ends of two safe strips. One extends farther: it is longer. Aishatu waits while John feels the aligned ends. Then they fold one paper circle into two equal matching parts: each is a half.','Use two safe strips. Align one end. Say which is longer, shorter or equal. Fold a paper circle into two equal matching parts. Explain why the parts are halves.','Comparison depends on strips; compare from one baseline. Two equal matching parts make halves.',None)]
